{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/356279-endowment-question","id":356279,"title":"Endowment Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-31T22:56:40-08:00","id":356279,"title":"Endowment Question","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I was curious if there are any Endowments or other kind of supernatural merit that allows a character to cast magic through rituals/incantations/grimoires to have effects like Spirit summoning/binding, mystical armor, wards &amp; the like? Witchfinders Gifted/Gnosis Mysteries come the closest to what I'm asking for (Benedictions &amp; Second Sight Thaumaturgy don't cover the same range of options I'm looking for) Mysteries seem too overt &amp; showy &amp; none of them seem to rely on books &amp; rituals of the occult or symbols &amp; sigils. Maybe i'm just not looking at it the right light but I was hoping someone could recommend me something that is more like Supernatural use of reading an incantation from a rare book &amp; drawing the sign of an angel/demon/pagan goddess/etc.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T00:12:47-08:00","id":356346,"title":"","content":"Check the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/11872/World-of-Darkness-Second-Sight?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Second Sight</b></a> - it get's witches and cultist that use magic based on individual Merits, not the tree of Mysteries. You could just also use the <b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">God Machine Rules Update</a> </b>(Totally free!), having some powers that could be re-fluffed as working from rituals - you just need to make the Extended Actions then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T19:39:44-08:00","id":357153,"title":"","content":"Actually no, the Witchfinders has exactly what you are looking for in that it has rules for anyone casting the mysteries as rituals, it's just something you need buddies and casting ingredients to do.<br /> <br /> In the mage chroniclers guide, it has a similar rule for anyone to cast arcana spells as rituals, requiring help, time, and ingredients.<br /> <br /> In Antagonists, it doesn't actually have rules, but it talks about occultists who can do folk magic.<br /> <br /> In Second Sight it has rules for thaumaturges casting rotes as rituals out of grimoires.<br /> <br /> Since the endowment system suggests using the reliquary system with it, you can build any endowment you want with the ritualistic and/or sacrificial costs, although those endowments would of course be limited to suitable conspiracies: cainites, inquisition, lucifuge, aegis, cheval, etc.<br /> <br /> Sorcery from Mirrors allows muggles to buy powers as merits, including the ritualistic powers of werewolves, vampire blood magic, sin-eater ceremonies, mage rituals, etc. Combining that with the reliquary bit above, you can allow sorcerers to have ritualistic versions of any power from nwod.<br /> <br /> Heck, you could have someone with the social merits with spirits like allies or contacts and the spirits require ritual appeasement to start using their numina and influences on the person's behalf, which would actually work with the occultist folk magic bit above. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 01-01-2015, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T00:36:14-08:00","id":357317,"title":"","content":"The last one could work out quite well. Just make up a chart giving &quot;levels&quot; to different favors, and you've got a decent little system right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T13:09:30-08:00","id":357678,"title":"","content":"Thank you StSword I think I'll definately check into those.<br /> <br /> Btw I don't think I explained myself well when I said &quot;ritual&quot; I didn't mean for it to take a long time. Just that it was more of asking some patron entity to do something rather than have the power yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}